{"id":"boaz","name":"Boaz","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:boaz"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Boaz","text":"Alacrity. (1.) The husband of Ruth, a wealthy Bethlehemite. By the “levirate law” the duty devolved on him of marrying Ruth the Moabitess (Ruth 4:1-13). He was a kinsman of Mahlon, her first husband. (2.) The name given (for what reason is unknown) to one of the two (the other was called Jachin) brazen pillars which Solomon erected in the court of the temple (1 Kings 7:21; 2 Chr. 3:17). These pillars were broken up and carried to Babylon by Nebuchadnezzar."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G1003","lemma":"Βοόζ","xlit":"Boóz","gloss":"Booz, , an Israelite","kjv":"Booz","count":2,"share":0.29},{"strong":"G5601","lemma":"Ὠβήδ","xlit":"Ōbḗd","gloss":"Obed, an Israelite","kjv":"Obed","count":2,"share":0.29},{"strong":"G4533","lemma":"Σαλμών","xlit":"Salmṓn","gloss":"Salmon, an Israelite","kjv":"Salmon","count":2,"share":0.29},{"strong":"G2421","lemma":"Ἰεσσαί","xlit":"Iessaí","gloss":"Jessæ , an Israelite","kjv":"Jesse","count":2,"share":0.29},{"strong":"H3199","lemma":"יָכִין","xlit":"Yâkîyn","gloss":"Jakin, the name of three Israelites and of a temple pill","kjv":"Jachin","count":2,"share":0.29},{"strong":"H8042","lemma":"שְׂמָאלִי","xlit":"sᵉmâʼlîy","gloss":"situated on the left side","kjv":"left","count":2,"share":0.29}],"verses":["Matt.1.5","Luke.3.32","Ruth.2.0","Ruth.3.0","Ruth.4.0","1Kgs.7.21","2Chr.3.17"],"related":[{"id":"naomi","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.375,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"lovers","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.25,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"widow","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.033,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"}],"works":[{"work":"kebra","title":"Kebra Nagast","count":1,"chapters":[{"chapter":"Kebra.16","count":1,"book":"Kebra N.","title":"Reuben"}]}]}
